# Law:      CLAUDE.md law 3 (asset refs in data are SOFT), law 7 (assets are generated by
#           committed scripts, never hand-placed).
# Doctrine: .claude/skills/ue-editor - the plan is the source of truth, the PNG and the
#           .uasset are its projection.
#
# THIS FILE IMPORTS NOTHING FROM UNREAL. Plain CPython 3.9+, stdlib only, so the whole plan
# can be validated and reviewed WITHOUT an editor:
#
#     python Tools/render_weapons/render_plan.py --verbose
#
# render_weapons.py (which does import unreal) imports this module and executes what it
# returns. Same split as Tools/gen_input and Tools/blockout: every decision is made here, in
# reviewable text; the editor half is a dumb executor plus the asserts only live assets can
# answer.
#
# DEPARTURE FROM THE PLAN DOCUMENT, RECORDED: section 4.1 called for the table to live in
# `weapon_render_profile.json` and deliberately skipped a `*_plan.py` split. It is inverted
# here - one Python file holding both the table and its validation - for one reason: the
# framing values below are UNVERIFIED GUESSES and JSON cannot carry the warning next to the
# number. When the spike has determined the real values and the warnings come off, moving
# the table back out to JSON is a mechanical change.
#
# Exit codes match the ladder convention (Tools/_BRLadderCommon.ps1):
#   0 PASS  plan is valid    1 FAIL  validation errors    3 BLOCKED  cannot read inputs
# =====================================================================================
